    "updated_at": "2025-03-14T05:48:39Z",
    "body": "I have a familiar use-case as @jlukic \n\nI want to open a popover using a synthetic long-press event, basically a context menu that opens when you long-press on an item.\n\nPseudo-code:\n\n```js\nlet timeout = null;\nfunction onPointerDown() {\n  timeout = setTimeout( dispatchEvent, 1000 );\n}\nfunction onPointerUpOrCancel() {\n  clearTimeout( timeout );\n}\n```\n\nThe issue is that the popover is opened on pointer down, then when the user releases it fires the click event and the popover closes.\n\nI tried setting `popover=\"manual\"` and closing the popover when the user clicks outside on the `::backdrop` (`event.target === event.currentTarget`), but the `::backdrop` has a user-agent style of `pointer-events: none !important`, which means this doesn't work.\n\nI'm going to give [this](https://stackoverflow.com/a/26984690) a try, but it's not ideal...",
