    "updated_at": "2025-05-26T11:46:04Z",
    "body": "I did. Sort of. But it isn't pretty.\n\nBelow is the (abstracted) preact component.\n\nThe idea is:\n\n- Set `popover=\"manual\"` so the popover doesn't auto-dismiss\n- Use `pointerup` / `-cancel` events on window to detect when the user releases the mouse/finger\n- Use `click` event on window to dismiss the popover IF `pointerup` / `-cancel` has fired at least once.\n\n```jsx\nfunction Popover() {\n\n  const preventPopoverClose = useSignal( _pointerIsDown() );\n\n  const ref = useRef();\n\n  useEffect(\n    () => {\n\n      const __onClick = event => !preventPopoverClose.peek() && ref.current.hidePopover();\n      const __onPointerUp = event => beforeNextPaint( () => preventPopoverClose.value = false );\n\n      on( 'click', window, __onClick );\n      on( 'pointerup pointercancel', window, __onPointerUp, { capture: true, once: true } );\n\n      return () => {\n        off( 'click', window, __onClick );\n        off( 'pointerup pointercancel', window, __onPointerUp );\n      };\n\n    },\n    [ preventPopoverClose ]\n  );\n\n  useEffect( () => ref.current.showPopover(), [] );\n\n  return (\n    <div ref={ ref } popover=\"manual\" />\n  );\n\n}\n\n/**\n * @private\n */\nfunction _pointerIsDown() {\n  return document.body.matches(':active');\n}\n```\n\nEDIT: `beforeNextPaint()` is a util function, basically a double-rAF.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
