    "created_at": "2025-12-01T23:39:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-01T23:39:25Z",
    "body": "> [@mfreed](https://github.com/mfreed) Yes, just means I need to re-implement light dismiss and auto-closing of other (non-toast) auto-popovers which is frustrating. `popover=auto` works perfectly for my use case _except_ for this one scenario.\n\nOh, I just re-read your comment. So you have some `popover=auto` popovers somewhere open on the screen, and you want a separate `popover=manual` toast that can be clicked directly without light-dismissing the first popovers? The reason that's not possible with the platform Popover is that it's very easy to get it wrong, and keep people from light dismissing popovers. The idea behind popovers generally is that they're ephemeral and can be easily closed. If there are a bunch of \"magic\" spots where clicks no longer light dismiss, users get confused. So yes, if you want this pattern, it does need to be manually implemented.",
