    "body": "@mfreed Right, but given that devs would still run into these exceptional cases the end result is the same user experience but now it's manually (and likely worse) implemented in JS which is the kind of thing the popover API was made to avoid.\n\nWhat if there were an easy way to opt in to the light dismiss logic of the browser? I didn't dive too deep into the CloseWatcher API, is that (the browser's internal CloseWatcher that is) something that could be exposed? Or maybe a `closedby` attribute similar to `<dialog>`.",
