    "created_at": "2025-12-02T20:14:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-02T20:15:54Z",
    "body": "> [CloseWatcher](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CloseWatcher) is likely not what you're looking for. That's about hooking into the default \"close\" button (ESC on a keyboard, back button on a mobile phone, etc.). And closedby adds the same kind of light dismiss to <dialog>; i.e. you can't \"poke holes\" in the light dismiss clickable area there either.\n\nRight okay, I somehow thought light dismiss (clicking outside) was part of `CloseWatcher` as well. I guess there's no equivalent for that (presumably because it's easy enough to do in JS and it's not platform-dependent). And `closedby` does include light dismiss, but that doesn't help me given that there's no programmatic way to hook into that for the same reason as `popover=\"auto\"`.\n\nI think in a way `CloseWatcher` _is_ what I'm looking for, because it would make re-implementing the `popover=\"auto\"` logic in JS much easier, namely by implementing both light dismiss (click outside, easy enough) + close (hard to do currently without `CloseWatcher`).",
